  "explanation": "The question asks for the establishment date of the 'Museum of Applied Arts'. Source D1S2 explicitly states: 'The museum was founded in 1874 as the \"Kunstgewerbemuseum\" (Museum of Arts and Crafts).' This refers to the institution now known as the Museum of Applied Arts (Leipzig), which received its present name in 2005 (D1S7). Source D2 describes the 'Museum of Applied Arts (Budapest)', noting it was built between 1893 and 1896 (D2S4), but does not provide a specific founding/establishment year for the museum itself, only construction dates. The date '1893' (Candidate C1) corresponds to the start of construction for the Budapest building, not the establishment of the museum entity. Therefore, only '1874' is the correct answer supported by the text for the establishment of the museum entity described in the primary source."
